Package: crossform
Title: Cross-Generalized Effect Geometry
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R: person("Bradley", "Buchsbaum", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "bradley.buchsbaum@gmail.com")
Description: Asks where task effects and representational geometries
    reproduce across independent partitions of a task functional magnetic
    resonance imaging (fMRI) dataset, such as separate runs or sessions. The
    effects, the spatial measurement, and the partitions that must generalize
    are declared once and compiled into a single estimand-bearing effect form;
    crossvalidated contrast energy, squared-distance representational
    dissimilarity matrices, fixed linear representational similarity analysis,
    and ordered cross-axis hypotheses are queries against that form rather
    than separate pipelines. Spatial measurements, generalization pairings,
    units, execution receipts, uncertainty capabilities, and principled
    refusals remain explicit.
